  "domain": "infrastructure",
  "definition": "Techniques for embedding imperceptible or visible signals into digital content\u2014such as text, images, audio, or AI-generated outputs\u2014to assert provenance, ownership, or authenticity. AI watermarking approaches include statistical token-distribution biasing (for large language models) and frequency-domain embedding (for images), enabling detection of machine-generated content and supporting intellectual property protection and content provenance verification.",
